Creating a Dataset for AI-Driven Magnet Design
To fine-tune a pre-trained model for designing particle accelerator magnets, you need a dataset that maps design requirements (inputs) to the corresponding magnet design parameters (outputs). Your existing design procedures, expressed in Python or other code, are the perfect tools for generating this dataset.

1. Understanding the Data Structure
Your dataset will consist of pairs of (Input Specifications, Output Design Parameters).

Input Specifications (Features - X): These are the variables that define the user's requirements for a magnet. They will be the input to your machine learning model.

Output Design Parameters (Labels - Y): These are the detailed design characteristics of the magnet that your existing procedures generate. They will be the target outputs for your machine learning model.

